I reproduced this independently on 2026-09-01 with Node.js 22.18.0 using @modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.29.0 and 1.30.0.

Results with a 300 ms protocol timeout:

SSE stream error: onerror fires at ~3-4 ms, but the request rejects only at ~304-306 ms with MCP error -32001: Request timed out.
Clean SSE EOF before the matching JSON-RPC response: no onerror callback, request rejects at ~301-302 ms.
application/json control response: resolves in ~1 ms.
So the transport observes the stream failure/EOF promptly, but the pending JSON-RPC request is not settled until the outer timeout. I also verified that returning the same response as application/json avoids the delay.

